1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,793
Behind them, the army of Pharaoh.

2
00:00:02,843 --> 00:00:04,778
In front of them, the sea.

3
00:00:04,828 --> 00:00:08,017
Thousands of people, with nowhere left to run.

4
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:09,294
And they cried out:

5
00:00:09,344 --> 00:00:11,641
"We are going to be overtaken!"

6
00:00:11,945 --> 00:00:13,892
But one man did not panic.

7
00:00:13,942 --> 00:00:17,038
Musa, alayhis salaam, said: "No!

8
00:00:17,088 --> 00:00:19,638
Indeed, with me is my Lord.

9
00:00:19,688 --> 00:00:21,324
He will guide me."

10
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:24,294
How did a baby who was meant to be killed...

11
00:00:24,344 --> 00:00:28,197
end up standing here, between a tyrant and the sea?

12
00:00:28,338 --> 00:00:32,514
This is the story of Prophet Musa, alayhis salaam,

13
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:36,242
the prophet the Quran speaks of more than any other.

14
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:37,703
From the river...

15
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:39,098
to the sea.

16
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,165
Egypt.

17
00:00:41,215 --> 00:00:42,593
The richest kingdom on earth,

18
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:45,449
ruled by a man who called himself a god.

19
00:00:45,499 --> 00:00:47,945
Pharaoh divided the people into classes.

20
00:00:47,995 --> 00:00:52,265
And one group, the Children of Israel, he crushed beneath his feet.

21
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:53,483
Allah says:

22
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:56,814
"Indeed, Pharaoh exalted himself in the land...

23
00:00:56,864 --> 00:01:01,390
slaughtering their newborn sons, and keeping their females alive."

24
00:01:01,601 --> 00:01:04,605
Every baby boy born to them was killed.

25
00:01:04,655 --> 00:01:06,963
Soldiers went from house to house.

26
00:01:07,046 --> 00:01:10,119
But Allah had a different plan. He says:

27
00:01:10,169 --> 00:01:14,601
"And We wanted to confer favour upon those who were oppressed in the land,

28
00:01:14,651 --> 00:01:18,363
and make them leaders, and make them inheritors."

29
00:01:18,413 --> 00:01:20,998
And the one who would bring Pharaoh down...

30
00:01:21,048 --> 00:01:24,936
was about to be born, inside his own kingdom.

31
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:29,640
In one of those homes, a mother gave birth to a son.

32
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:31,476
And she was terrified.

33
00:01:31,559 --> 00:01:33,680
Then Allah inspired her:

34
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:36,989
"When you fear for him, cast him into the river.

35
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:39,613
And do not fear, and do not grieve.

36
00:01:39,663 --> 00:01:42,167
Indeed, We will return him to you,

37
00:01:42,217 --> 00:01:44,582
and make him one of the messengers."

38
00:01:44,632 --> 00:01:46,718
So she placed her baby in a basket,

39
00:01:46,768 --> 00:01:48,634
and gave him to the river.

40
00:01:48,684 --> 00:01:50,062
The river carried him...

41
00:01:50,112 --> 00:01:52,384
straight to the palace of Pharaoh.

42
00:01:52,434 --> 00:01:54,905
And the family of Pharaoh picked him up.

43
00:01:55,116 --> 00:01:57,701
Pharaoh's wife looked at the baby and said:

44
00:01:57,751 --> 00:02:00,907
"A comfort of the eye for me and for you.

45
00:02:00,991 --> 00:02:02,707
Do not kill him."

46
00:02:03,104 --> 00:02:05,921
Back at home, his mother's heart became empty.

47
00:02:05,971 --> 00:02:09,081
His sister followed the basket from a distance.

48
00:02:09,222 --> 00:02:12,376
And the baby refused every nurse in the palace...

49
00:02:12,426 --> 00:02:13,944
until his sister said:

50
00:02:13,994 --> 00:02:17,009
shall I show you a family who will take care of him?

51
00:02:17,059 --> 00:02:19,818
And so Allah returned him to his mother,

52
00:02:19,868 --> 00:02:23,651
"so that she would know that the promise of Allah is true."

53
00:02:23,735 --> 00:02:26,390
The child Pharaoh feared most...

54
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:29,259
grew up in Pharaoh's own house.

55
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,719
Years passed.

56
00:02:31,769 --> 00:02:34,482
Musa grew into a strong young man,

57
00:02:34,532 --> 00:02:37,456
and Allah gave him wisdom and knowledge.

58
00:02:37,539 --> 00:02:41,752
One day he entered the city, and found two men fighting.

59
00:02:41,893 --> 00:02:45,212
One from his own people, and one from his enemy.

60
00:02:45,295 --> 00:02:48,033
The man from his people called to him for help.

61
00:02:48,175 --> 00:02:50,702
Musa struck the other man once...

62
00:02:50,752 --> 00:02:52,399
and the man died.

63
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:55,451
He had never meant to kill him. He said:

64
00:02:55,501 --> 00:02:58,260
"This is from the work of Satan."

65
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:00,663
And he turned to his Lord at once:

66
00:03:00,713 --> 00:03:03,903
"My Lord, indeed I have wronged myself,

67
00:03:03,953 --> 00:03:07,771
so forgive me." And Allah forgave him.

68
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:09,536
But the news spread.

69
00:03:09,677 --> 00:03:12,844
And a man came running from the far end of the city:

70
00:03:13,241 --> 00:03:17,674
"O Musa, the chiefs are planning to kill you. Leave!"

71
00:03:17,757 --> 00:03:22,572
So he left Egypt alone, afraid, looking over his shoulder.

72
00:03:22,622 --> 00:03:24,035
And he prayed:

73
00:03:24,085 --> 00:03:27,728
"My Lord, save me from the wrongdoing people."

74
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,758
He walked across the desert for days,

75
00:03:30,808 --> 00:03:35,601
with no food and no shelter, until he reached the land of Madyan.

76
00:03:35,905 --> 00:03:39,001
At the well, shepherds crowded around the water.

77
00:03:39,051 --> 00:03:43,554
And standing apart, he saw two women holding back their flock.

78
00:03:43,637 --> 00:03:46,758
He asked them what was wrong. They said:

79
00:03:46,842 --> 00:03:50,265
we cannot water our sheep until the shepherds leave.

80
00:03:50,348 --> 00:03:53,051
And our father is a very old man.

81
00:03:53,192 --> 00:03:56,023
So Musa watered their flock for them.

82
00:03:56,234 --> 00:04:00,933
Then he went back to the shade of a tree. Exhausted. Hungry.

83
00:04:00,983 --> 00:04:02,848
A stranger with nothing.

84
00:04:02,898 --> 00:04:04,346
And he made a dua:

85
00:04:04,396 --> 00:04:06,401
"My Lord, indeed I am,

86
00:04:06,451 --> 00:04:10,244
for whatever good You would send down to me, in need."

87
00:04:10,294 --> 00:04:12,798
And Allah answered him almost at once.

88
00:04:12,848 --> 00:04:18,162
Their father invited him in, heard his story, and told him: "Fear not.

89
00:04:18,212 --> 00:04:21,101
You have escaped from the wrongdoing people."

90
00:04:21,184 --> 00:04:25,395
He gave Musa work, a home, and his daughter in marriage.

91
00:04:25,445 --> 00:04:29,030
And Musa stayed in Madyan for years.

92
00:04:30,030 --> 00:04:31,582
When his term was complete,

93
00:04:31,632 --> 00:04:34,914
Musa set out with his family, back toward Egypt.

94
00:04:34,964 --> 00:04:37,979
It was a cold, dark night in the desert.

95
00:04:38,029 --> 00:04:41,812
Then, on the side of the mountain, he saw a fire.

96
00:04:41,895 --> 00:04:44,657
He told his family: stay here.

97
00:04:44,798 --> 00:04:46,582
Perhaps I can bring you some news,

98
00:04:46,632 --> 00:04:49,729
or a burning stick, so you can warm yourselves.

99
00:04:49,779 --> 00:04:52,180
But when he came to it, he was called:

100
00:04:52,263 --> 00:04:56,184
"Indeed, I am your Lord, so remove your sandals.

101
00:04:56,234 --> 00:04:59,866
Indeed, you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa."

102
00:05:00,007 --> 00:05:02,047
"Indeed, I am Allah.

103
00:05:02,097 --> 00:05:04,078
There is no deity except Me,

104
00:05:04,128 --> 00:05:07,876
so worship Me, and establish prayer for My remembrance."

105
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,558
Then Allah asked:

106
00:05:09,608 --> 00:05:13,796
"And what is that in your right hand, O Musa?" He said:

107
00:05:13,846 --> 00:05:15,423
it is my staff.

108
00:05:15,727 --> 00:05:19,196
I lean on it, and I bring down leaves for my sheep.

109
00:05:19,337 --> 00:05:23,688
"Throw it down, O Musa." So he threw it down...

110
00:05:23,738 --> 00:05:26,137
and it was a snake, moving swiftly.

111
00:05:26,187 --> 00:05:28,332
"Seize it, and fear not.

112
00:05:28,382 --> 00:05:31,120
We will return it to its former state."

113
00:05:31,261 --> 00:05:33,184
And then came the command:

114
00:05:33,234 --> 00:05:34,659
"Go to Pharaoh.

115
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:37,528
Indeed, he has transgressed."

116
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:40,105
Go to Pharaoh.

117
00:05:40,155 --> 00:05:41,998
The man who wanted him dead.

118
00:05:42,048 --> 00:05:44,113
The man he had run from.

119
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,212
Musa did not refuse.

120
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:50,034
But he knew his weakness, and he asked his Lord for help:

121
00:05:50,094 --> 00:05:53,120
"My Lord, expand for me my chest.

122
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:55,361
And ease for me my task.

123
00:05:55,411 --> 00:06:00,320
And untie the knot from my tongue, so they may understand my speech."

124
00:06:00,404 --> 00:06:03,488
"And appoint for me a helper from my family:

125
00:06:03,538 --> 00:06:05,800
Harun, my brother."

126
00:06:05,942 --> 00:06:09,096
And Allah gave him everything he asked for.

127
00:06:09,146 --> 00:06:10,907
Then He told them both:

128
00:06:10,957 --> 00:06:13,461
"Speak to him with gentle speech,

129
00:06:13,511 --> 00:06:17,085
that perhaps he may be reminded, or fear."

130
00:06:17,226 --> 00:06:18,303
Gentle words...

131
00:06:18,353 --> 00:06:20,777
to the worst tyrant on earth.

132
00:06:21,081 --> 00:06:24,293
If Allah asked for gentleness with Pharaoh,

133
00:06:24,343 --> 00:06:27,093
how gently should we speak to each other?

134
00:06:27,176 --> 00:06:28,403
They were afraid.

135
00:06:28,453 --> 00:06:31,342
And Allah said: "Fear not.

136
00:06:31,425 --> 00:06:33,931
Indeed, I am with you both.

137
00:06:34,073 --> 00:06:36,462
I hear, and I see."

138
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:41,218
So Musa and Harun walked into the palace of Pharaoh.

139
00:06:41,268 --> 00:06:44,250
The same palace where Musa had grown up.

140
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:45,386
They said:

141
00:06:45,436 --> 00:06:47,872
we are messengers of your Lord.

142
00:06:47,955 --> 00:06:52,365
Let the Children of Israel go with us, and do not torment them.

143
00:06:52,507 --> 00:06:54,037
Pharaoh mocked him:

144
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:57,531
did we not raise you among us as a child?

145
00:06:57,614 --> 00:06:59,575
And then you did what you did.

146
00:06:59,786 --> 00:07:02,222
Musa showed him the signs.

147
00:07:02,305 --> 00:07:04,730
But Pharaoh only grew prouder.

148
00:07:04,871 --> 00:07:07,119
He gathered his people and announced:

149
00:07:07,169 --> 00:07:09,722
"I am your most exalted lord."

150
00:07:09,863 --> 00:07:12,032
And he called it all magic.

151
00:07:12,173 --> 00:07:14,738
We will bring you magic like it, he said.

152
00:07:14,821 --> 00:07:17,255
Let us meet on the day of the festival,

153
00:07:17,305 --> 00:07:19,277
in front of all the people.

154
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:24,307
On the day of the festival, the whole city came to watch.

155
00:07:24,448 --> 00:07:27,383
Pharaoh brought the best magicians in Egypt.

156
00:07:27,525 --> 00:07:28,717
Musa said:

157
00:07:28,767 --> 00:07:30,203
you throw first.

158
00:07:30,253 --> 00:07:33,175
And they threw down their ropes and their staffs.

159
00:07:33,225 --> 00:07:37,484
And by their magic, they seemed to be moving, like snakes.

160
00:07:37,568 --> 00:07:40,677
Even Musa felt a fear inside himself.

161
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,044
Allah said: "Fear not.

162
00:07:43,094 --> 00:07:45,691
Indeed, it is you who are superior.

163
00:07:45,741 --> 00:07:48,340
And throw what is in your right hand."

164
00:07:48,643 --> 00:07:50,370
Musa threw his staff.

165
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:53,249
And it swallowed up everything they had made.

166
00:07:53,299 --> 00:07:56,256
The magicians knew magic better than anyone.

167
00:07:56,306 --> 00:07:57,324
And they knew:

168
00:07:57,374 --> 00:07:59,019
this was not magic.

169
00:07:59,069 --> 00:08:01,690
They fell down in prostration, all of them,

170
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:03,849
in front of Pharaoh, and said:

171
00:08:03,899 --> 00:08:07,415
"We have believed in the Lord of Harun and Musa."

172
00:08:07,556 --> 00:08:09,178
Pharaoh was furious.

173
00:08:09,228 --> 00:08:11,616
He threatened to cut off their hands and feet,

174
00:08:11,666 --> 00:08:14,706
and crucify them on the trunks of palm trees.

175
00:08:14,848 --> 00:08:16,028
They answered:

176
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:19,941
"Never will we prefer you over the clear proofs that have come to us,

177
00:08:19,991 --> 00:08:22,357
and over the One who created us.

178
00:08:22,661 --> 00:08:24,828
So decree whatever you will.

179
00:08:24,878 --> 00:08:28,265
You can only decree for this worldly life."

180
00:08:28,315 --> 00:08:30,598
They came that morning as magicians.

181
00:08:30,648 --> 00:08:32,841
They left as believers.

182
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:37,180
Still, Pharaoh and his chiefs refused.

183
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:40,234
So Allah sent them sign after sign.

184
00:08:40,284 --> 00:08:43,159
"So We sent upon them the flood, and locusts,

185
00:08:43,209 --> 00:08:47,967
and lice, and frogs, and blood, as distinct signs."

186
00:08:48,109 --> 00:08:51,437
Each time a sign came, they begged Musa:

187
00:08:51,487 --> 00:08:53,585
pray to your Lord for us.

188
00:08:53,635 --> 00:08:55,919
If you remove it, we will believe,

189
00:08:55,969 --> 00:08:58,229
and let the Children of Israel go.

190
00:08:58,279 --> 00:09:01,805
And each time it was lifted, they broke their promise.

191
00:09:01,855 --> 00:09:04,872
But they were arrogant, and a criminal people.

192
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:08,214
Until at last, Allah inspired Musa:

193
00:09:08,264 --> 00:09:10,988
"Travel by night with My servants.

194
00:09:11,038 --> 00:09:13,614
Indeed, you will be pursued."

195
00:09:14,610 --> 00:09:18,287
In the dark of night, the Children of Israel left Egypt.

196
00:09:18,337 --> 00:09:20,552
Men, women and children.

197
00:09:20,694 --> 00:09:24,893
At sunrise, Pharaoh came after them with his whole army.

198
00:09:24,943 --> 00:09:27,702
And now we are back where we began.

199
00:09:27,752 --> 00:09:29,456
The sea in front of them.

200
00:09:29,506 --> 00:09:31,139
The army behind.

201
00:09:31,189 --> 00:09:34,599
"We are going to be overtaken!" "No!

202
00:09:34,649 --> 00:09:37,258
Indeed, with me is my Lord.

203
00:09:37,308 --> 00:09:39,001
He will guide me."

204
00:09:39,212 --> 00:09:41,577
Then Allah inspired Musa:

205
00:09:41,627 --> 00:09:45,570
"Strike with your staff the sea." And it parted.

206
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:48,891
And each side was like a great, towering mountain.

207
00:09:48,941 --> 00:09:51,979
A dry path opened through the middle of the sea.

208
00:09:52,029 --> 00:09:55,824
And they walked across, all of them, without fear.

209
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:58,430
Pharaoh saw the path,

210
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:02,308
and followed them into the sea, with all his soldiers.

211
00:10:02,358 --> 00:10:05,769
And when the last of the Children of Israel had crossed...

212
00:10:05,853 --> 00:10:09,019
the sea closed over Pharaoh and his army.

213
00:10:09,069 --> 00:10:10,574
As the water overtook him,

214
00:10:10,624 --> 00:10:13,699
the man who had called himself a god cried out:

215
00:10:13,782 --> 00:10:19,247
"I believe that there is no deity except the One in whom the Children of Israel believe,

216
00:10:19,297 --> 00:10:21,570
and I am of the Muslims."

217
00:10:21,711 --> 00:10:24,494
But it was too late. "Now?

218
00:10:24,544 --> 00:10:28,734
And you had disobeyed before, and were of the corrupters."

219
00:10:28,817 --> 00:10:32,296
"So today We will save you in body,

220
00:10:32,346 --> 00:10:35,897
that you may be a sign to those who come after you."

221
00:10:36,410 --> 00:10:40,667
The tyrant who killed the babies of Bani Israel was drowned...

222
00:10:40,717 --> 00:10:45,139
in the same water that once carried baby Musa to safety.

223
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,890
A baby in a basket.

224
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,258
A stranger alone at a well.

225
00:10:50,308 --> 00:10:53,870
A shepherd with a staff, standing before a king.

226
00:10:53,954 --> 00:10:56,887
Every time, it looked like Musa had nothing.

227
00:10:56,937 --> 00:10:59,407
And every time, Allah was with him.

228
00:10:59,457 --> 00:11:02,541
When he was afraid, Allah said: fear not.

229
00:11:02,591 --> 00:11:04,446
When he was alone, he said:

230
00:11:04,496 --> 00:11:06,584
my Lord, I am in need.

231
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:09,124
And when the sea was in front of him, he said:

232
00:11:09,174 --> 00:11:10,042
"No!

233
00:11:10,092 --> 00:11:12,515
Indeed, with me is my Lord.

234
00:11:12,565 --> 00:11:14,107
He will guide me."

235
00:11:14,318 --> 00:11:17,950
Whatever is behind you, and whatever is in front of you...

236
00:11:18,033 --> 00:11:20,074
your Lord is with you too.

237
00:11:20,285 --> 00:11:24,555
If this story moved you, subscribe to Haq Stories.

238
00:11:24,639 --> 00:11:28,214
And watch the complete story of Prophet Yusuf next.
